This is my attempt to make EFL work on 2.11 BSD.  The 64K memory space makes
this a dicey proposition at best.  I was motivated by the fact that the
system includes an installed man page for EFL, but no binary.  4.3 BSD includes
both the man page and the binary, so (in my mind) it was worth a try.

Most of the changes were confined to a new Makefile.  I managed to squeeze
EFL into a split I&D (411) binary, a minor miracle.  This was done by
carefully ordering the object files and by rewriting the error message
printing code in error.c.  Over 2000 bytes are now part of an external
messages file, efl_errorstrings.  This makes the binary just barely fit.
As a reminder, I have added a new program, catastrophe, which prints
the number of bytes remaining in the text and data segments. If catastrophe
fails, well, the program may need restructuring into an overlaid executable.

Good Luck and God Speed,

Frank Wortner
